### Types (`lib/types.ts`)
```ts
export interface ChatMessage {
  id: string;
  role: ChatMessageRole;
  content: string;
  timestamp: number;
  controlRequest?: { ... };
  userQuestion?: { ... };
}
```

`AssistantContentBlock` can be:
- `{ type: "text"; text: string }`
- `{ type: "tool_use"; id: string; name: string; input: Record<string, unknown> }`
- `{ type: "tool_result"; tool_use_id: string; content: string }`

## Requirements
Design a condenser that groups consecutive tool-call messages into a single collapsible summary. When Claude does 5 Grep calls in a row, instead of 5 separate messages, show something like "5 tool calls (Grep x3, Read x2)" that can be expanded to see details.

## Design Constraints
- Should work at the rendering layer (in chat.tsx or a new component), NOT by modifying the underlying message data
- Keep the raw view unaffected
- The condenser should be a utility/component that groups consecutive tool-only assistant messages
- Messages with actual text content from Claude should NOT be condensed
- Control requests and user questions should break the condensing sequence

Please design a detailed implementation plan covering:
1. How to detect "tool-only" messages (messages that only have tool_use/tool_result blocks, no real text)
2. How to group consecutive tool-only messages
3. The condensed UI component
4. Where the grouping logic lives (utility function vs inline in chat.tsx)
5. Any type changes needed

