{displayItems.map((item) => {
  if (item.kind === "condensed") {
    return <CondensedToolGroup key={item.id} group={item} />;
  }

  const msg = item.message;
  return msg.userQuestion ? (
    <UserQuestion key={msg.id} message={msg} onRespond={onRespondToUserQuestion} />
  ) : msg.controlRequest ? (
    <ControlRequest key={msg.id} message={msg} onRespond={onRespondToControl} />
  ) : (
    <Message key={msg.id} message={msg} />
  );
})}
```

The `useMemo` ensures the condensing logic only re-runs when the `messages` array reference changes (which happens on every new message). This is efficient because `condenseMessages` is a single linear pass -- O(n).

### 8. Raw View Unaffected

The raw view (`showRaw` toggle) renders from `rawMessages` (a separate `ClaudeMessage[]`), not from `messages`. The condenser only affects the `messages` rendering path. No changes needed for raw view.

### 9. File Summary and Sequencing

The implementation involves changes to 4 existing files and creation of 2 new files, in this order:

**Step 1 -- Types** (`/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/lib/types.ts`):
- Add `ToolCallInfo` interface
- Add optional `toolCalls?: ToolCallInfo[]` and `isToolOnly?: boolean` fields to `ChatMessage`

**Step 2 -- Message enrichment** (`/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/hooks/use-websocket.ts`):
- Import `ToolCallInfo` type
- Modify the `assistant` branch in `relayChatMessage()` to compute and attach `toolCalls` and `isToolOnly`
- No changes to `extractText()` (it still produces the same display text)

**Step 3 -- Grouping utility** (new file: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/lib/condense-messages.ts`):
- Export `SingleItem`, `CondensedGroup`, `DisplayItem` types
- Export `condenseMessages()` pure function

**Step 4 -- Condensed group component** (new file: `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/condensed-tool-group.tsx`):
- Collapsible summary bar with expand/collapse
- Reuses existing `Message` component for expanded view

**Step 5 -- Chat integration** (`/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/chat.tsx`):
- Import `condenseMessages` and `CondensedToolGroup`
- Add `useMemo` call to produce `displayItems`
- Replace `messages.map(...)` with `displayItems.map(...)`

### 10. Edge Cases and Considerations

**Mixed messages**: A single `ClaudeAssistant` message might contain both text blocks and tool_use blocks (e.g., Claude says "Let me search for that" and then runs Grep in the same message). These have `isToolOnly === false` because they contain meaningful text. They render as normal messages and break the condensing sequence. This is correct behavior.

**Streaming / incremental updates**: The current architecture already handles this correctly. Each NDJSON line from the CLI produces a new `ChatMessage` (the assistant branch in `relayChatMessage` is called per relay). The last message for a given assistant turn is the complete one (stop_reason is set). The condenser works on the full `messages` array, so as new messages arrive, the condensed groups update naturally.

**Messages with only `tool_result` blocks**: These would have `toolCalls` as empty (since `tool_result` is not `tool_use`), but they would still have `isToolOnly === false` since the check requires `toolCalls.length > 0`. Actually, looking at the code more carefully, `tool_result` blocks also result in content like `[tool_result: ...]`, so `textBlocks.length === 0` would be true and `toolCalls.length > 0` would be false. The message would NOT be marked `isToolOnly`. This means standalone tool_result messages just render normally as before. This is acceptable -- tool_results usually come in the same assistant message as tool_use blocks in practice.

**Performance**: `condenseMessages` is O(n) where n is the number of messages. Wrapped in `useMemo`, it only re-runs when the messages array changes. Even with hundreds of messages, this is negligible.

**Accessibility**: The expand/collapse button should get an `aria-expanded` attribute and an `aria-label` for screen readers. Add to the button in `CondensedToolGroup`:

```tsx
aria-expanded={expanded}
aria-label={`${group.summary}, click to ${expanded ? "collapse" : "expand"}`}
```

### 11. Alternative Considered and Rejected

**Regex-based detection at render time**: Parse `content` with a regex like `/^\[tool_(use|result):.*\]$/` per line. This is fragile -- if the text format of `extractText` changes, the regex breaks. Adding structured metadata (`toolCalls`, `isToolOnly`) to `ChatMessage` is more robust and self-documenting.

**Modifying message data in useWebSocket**: The requirement says the condenser should work at the rendering layer. Adding metadata to `ChatMessage` at creation time is a minor hook change, but the actual grouping/condensing happens entirely in the rendering layer. The underlying `messages` array is unchanged -- still the same `ChatMessage[]` with the same content strings. The raw view is completely unaffected.

---

### Critical Files for Implementation

- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/lib/types.ts` - Add `ToolCallInfo` interface and `toolCalls`/`isToolOnly` optional fields to `ChatMessage`
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/hooks/use-websocket.ts` - Enrich `relayChatMessage()` to populate `toolCalls` and `isToolOnly` on assistant messages
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/lib/condense-messages.ts` - New file: pure grouping function that transforms `ChatMessage[]` into `DisplayItem[]`
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/chat.tsx` - Integrate `condenseMessages()` via `useMemo` and update the rendering loop
- `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/personal/thos/components/dashboard/condensed-tool-group.tsx` - New file: collapsible UI component for grouped tool-call messages

